## Summary

All five checklist items (CHK-0026 through CHK-0030) are **out-of-scope** for the target file `/home/gohan/runners/security-agent-1/_work/security-agent/security-agent/target_workspace/beacon-chain/execution/engine_client.go`, function `Service.NewPayload` (lines 144-202).

The root cause is a **layer mismatch**: the checklist items were generated from EVM execution-layer specifications (nonce management, gas accounting, EIP-1559 fee routing, SELFDESTRUCT), but they were mapped to the Prysm consensus client, which implements none of these concerns. Prysm's `NewPayload` function is a sealed JSON-RPC proxy:

1. It serializes an `ExecutionData` payload (one of three versioned proto types)
2. It calls `engine_newPayloadV1/V2/V3/V4` on the attached execution engine
3. It interprets the returned `PayloadStatus` and surfaces errors to the caller

No EVM state — nonces, balances, gas accounting, coinbase credits, or account deletion — is instantiated, modified, or validated in Prysm. All such logic lives in the execution engine (e.g., go-ethereum, reth) on the other side of the Engine API. These checklist items should be re-scoped to the appropriate execution client codebase.

